Slack demo screen

A design system for rendering Slack as one surface inside a self-contained HTML demo prototype. The baseline values come from the Stellar Media demo build (September 2026), which was matched against real Slack screenshots. The rail and top bar were rebuilt in November 2026 from Slack's own icon paths and checked against the real client (see Rail and top bar). Anything not listed here is not verified: ask for a screenshot of the real screen instead of approximating.

Ask before building
Workspace name, and the initials for the workspace tile.
Persona name and role (the person sending the prompt).
Where the exchange happens: Slackbot DM panel (default), an agent DM, a channel, or a channel thread.
Channel names and a few lines of realistic channel discussion tied to the use case.
The prompt, the tool or action line, the response text, and any widget content.
Hard rules
Never redraw brand marks. Slack, Slackbot, Salesforce, Auth0 and other logos must come from assets the user supplies (or an official source) and be embedded as base64. If an asset is missing, ask for it. The Slackbot avatar used before was the user's own GIF, embedded so it blinks.
Spell the workspace name exactly as given, everywhere: search placeholder, sidebar header, channel names.
No empty or default channels. Name channels for the use case (for example #stellarfest-event-ops, #ticketing-ops) and seed them with believable discussion.
A Slackbot DM has no tab row. Its header is: avatar, name, then history (clock), boxed compose, kebab, close, with a hairline underneath and messages starting directly below. Channels do keep their Messages / Add canvas tabs.
The top bar's right side shows the Slackbot avatar (28px, radius 7px) and the help icon in Slackbot demos. In agent or channel demos with no Slackbot, show the help icon only.
No lower thirds, overlays or prototype control chips (scenario toggles, failure-mode switches) on the Slack screen unless asked.
Keep the screen true to Slack. Demo content lives only in messages and widgets.
Rail and top bar glyphs must be Slack's real icon paths (see Rail and top bar). Never substitute generic or hand-drawn icons.
Unread counts use Slack's mention badge (see Badges). Never lay a dot over the icon, and never draw the badge inside the icon box. The rail Activity badge sits on the icon's top-right corner, pushed outward so it barely covers the glyph.
Render Slack markdown properly: bold in a message is shown bold, never with literal asterisks.
Layout

Full-window, column flex:

Top bar, 40px, aubergine: back / forward / history at left 300px, centered search ("Search <Workspace>"), Slackbot avatar and help at right.
Body, row flex on aubergine:
Rail, 70px: workspace tile, Home (selected), DMs, Activity, Files, To-dos, Agents & tools, then plus, moon and the user avatar with a green presence dot pinned to the bottom.
Panes, white, 6px radius, inset 4px from the right and bottom edges:
Sidebar, 260px: workspace name with chevron, setup pill, "Find a conversation", Threads / Huddles / Recap / Drafts & sent / Directories, separator, Starred, Salesforce group, Channels, Direct messages, footer, "Unread mentions" pill.
Main channel: 52px header, 40px tabs, messages, composer.
Slackbot or agent panel on the right: 56% width, min 560px, 52px header, messages, composer. A thread panel uses 50% width, min 600px (see Thread panel).
