Base CSS

Prefix every class with sl- so it cannot collide with other surfaces in the same file (a bare .dd class collided with a settings dropdown once; it became .sdd).

css
.sl{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:200;display:none;font-family:'Lato',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#1d1c1d;background:#fff}
.sl.on{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
/* top bar, body and rail rules: see "Rail and top bar" below (verified) */
.sl-panes{flex:1;display:flex;min-width:0;background:#fff;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;margin:0 4px 4px 0}
.sl-side{width:260px;background:#3f0e40;color:#e8dfe8;flex-shrink:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:10px 0 0}
.sl-side .h{display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 14px 8px;font-weight:900;font-size:17px;color:#fff;gap:6px}
.sl-side .setup{margin:2px 12px 10px;height:44px;border:1px solid #7b5a7c;border-radius:9px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:0 12px;font-size:14px;color:#fff}
.sl-side .find{margin:0 12px 10px;height:30px;border:1px solid #7b5a7c;border-radius:6px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:0 10px;font-size:13.5px;color:#cfc3cf}
.sl-side a{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:5px 14px 5px 18px;font-size:14.5px;color:#cfc3cf;white-space:nowrap}
.sl-side a.on{background:#fff;color:#350d36;font-weight:700;border-radius:6px;margin:0 8px;padding-left:10px}
.sl-side a.b{color:#fff;font-weight:700}
.sl-side a .badge{margin-left:auto;background:#cd2553;color:#fff;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;border-radius:9px;padding:1px 7px}
.sl-side .dav{width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:5px;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:7.5px;letter-spacing:-.2px;font-weight:900;color:#fff;position:relative;flex-shrink:0}
.sl-side .dav.pr:after{content:"";position:absolute;right:-3px;bottom:-3px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#2bac76;border:2px solid #3f0e40}
.sl-side .dav.aw:after{content:"";position:absolute;right:-3px;bottom:-3px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#3f0e40;border:1.5px solid #cfc3cf}
.sl-side .sec{padding:12px 14px 4px;font-size:14px;color:#cfc3cf;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.sl-side .sep{height:1px;background:#6b4a6c;margin:10px 0}
.sl-side .unread{margin:8px 12px 14px;background:#e8d5ea;color:#350d36;border-radius:22px;padding:8px 14px;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;text-align:center}
.sl-main{flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;border-right:1px solid #ddd}
.sl-ch{height:52px;border-bottom:1px solid #e3e3e3;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 16px;gap:10px;font-weight:900;font-size:17px}
.sl-tabs{height:40px;border-bottom:1px solid #e3e3e3;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 16px;gap:18px;font-size:13.5px;color:#616061}
.sl-tabs span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:11px 0}
.sl-tabs span.on{color:#1d1c1d;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #7d4d7f}
.sl-msgs{flex:1;overflow-y:auto;padding:22px 20px 12px;min-height:0}
.sl-date{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:10px 0 14px}
.sl-date:before,.sl-date:after{content:"";flex:1;height:1px;background:#e3e3e3}
.sl-date span{border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:20px;padding:5px 12px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700}
.sl-m{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:8px;border-radius:8px;position:relative}
.sl-m .av{width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;flex-shrink:0;overflow:hidden}
.sl-m .who{font-weight:900;font-size:15px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px}
.sl-m .who small{font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:#616061}
.sl-m .txt{font-size:15px;line-height:1.46;margin-top:2px}
.sl-m .txt+.txt{margin-top:10px}
.sl-m .used{font-size:13.5px;color:#616061;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin:3px 0 10px}
.sl-typing{font-size:13px;color:#616061;padding:6px 8px 0 54px;display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center}
.sl-typing i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:#9a9a9a;animation:sl-tdot 1s infinite}
.sl-typing i:nth-child(2){animation-delay:.2s}.sl-typing i:nth-child(3){animation-delay:.4s}
@keyframes sl-tdot{0%,100%{opacity:.3;transform:translateY(0)}50%{opacity:1;transform:translateY(-3px)}}
.sl-comp{margin:0 20px 18px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden}
.sl-comp .tb{height:38px;background:#f8f8f8;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:0 12px;color:#9a9a9a;font-weight:700;font-size:15px}
.sl-comp .fld{padding:10px 14px;min-height:44px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;outline:none}
.sl-comp .fld.empty:before{content:attr(data-ph);color:#8d8d8d}
.sl-comp .bb{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:6px 10px 8px;color:#616061;font-size:15px}
.sl-send{margin-left:auto;width:34px;height:28px;border-radius:5px;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#aaa;cursor:pointer;transition:background .2s,color .2s}
.sl-send.ready{background:#007a5a;color:#fff}
.sl-send+.sdd{width:20px;height:28px;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#aaa;border-left:1px solid #ddd}
.sl-bot{width:56%;min-width:560px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:#fff;flex-shrink:0}
.sl-bot .hd{height:52px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:0 20px;font-weight:900;font-size:19px;border-bottom:1px solid #e3e3e3}
.sl-bot .hd .ic{margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:22px;color:#1d1c1d;font-weight:400;font-size:18px}
.sl-bot .sl-msgs{padding:40px 20px 12px}
.slbot-logo{width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:8px;flex-shrink:0}

Interface icons outside the rail and top bar (not brand marks) are 24-viewBox line icons: no fill, currentColor stroke, stroke-width 1.8, round caps and joins. The rail and top bar are the exception: they use Slack's real filled icon paths (see Rail and top bar). If the user supplies more of Slack's real icon paths, those replace the line icons too.

Rail and top bar (verified against the real Slack client, November 2026)

The user supplied an HTML export of their live Slack desktop client plus a 2x rail screenshot. The glyphs below are Slack's own 20-viewBox icon paths, copied from that export. Their data-qa names are home, direct-messages, notifications, canvas-browser-filled, check-circle, ai-agents, plus, moon, arrow-left, arrow-right, clock, search and help-icon. Ignore any customer branding, workspace logos, avatars or user names in such exports; never copy them into a demo. The user rejected two earlier icon sets as "not right": thin generic line icons, then a hand-drawn Slack-style set. Never substitute generic or hand-drawn icons.

Measured from the 2x screenshot, at 1x:

Rail 70px wide (--tab-rail-width: 70px), top nav 40px, sidebar 260px (--sidebar-width: 260px), 4px client padding with 6px radius on the panes.
Rail order: Home, DMs, Activity, Files, To-dos, Agents & tools. Each item takes 68px of height: a 36x36 icon tile with an 8px radius, then the label.
Icons are 20px with fill="currentColor" and evenodd paths. They are not stroked.
Rail background 
#38123c. Icons and labels 
#baaebd, including on the selected tab. The selected tile is 
#56355c, and the selected tab uses the filled glyph.
Labels are 11px, weight 700, line-height 13px. "Agents & tools" breaks as "Agents<br>& tools".
An unread item with no mentions gets a dimmed dot (
#7a607d, about 9px) at the icon's top-right; this is b.dot.
Filled Home is derived from the outline: its outer contour is filled and the window is cut out with evenodd. Slack's own home-filled path was not in the export. The selected Files glyph in the export, canvas-browser-filled, is real; the Files glyph below is the outline variant from the sidebar list. A filled bell (Activity selected) and filled bubbles (DMs selected) were not in the export, so ask for them before showing those tabs selected.

